ellulosic biopolymers, polyvinyl butyral sheets, polyester films and window and protective films for value-added end uses in the transportation, durables, electronics, building and construction, medical and pharma, and consumables end-markets. The company's Chemical Intermediates segment offers olefin and acetyl derivatives, methylamines and salts, higher amines and solvents, ethylene, and commodity solvents; and primary non-phthalate and phthalate plasticizers, and niche non-phthalate plasticizers for industrial chemicals and processing, building and construction, health and wellness, and food and feed. Its Fibers segment provides cellulose acetate tow, triacetin, cellulose acetate flake, acetic acid, and acetic anhydride for use in filtration media primarily cigarette filters; natural and solution dyed acetate yarns, and staple fiber for use in consumables, and health and wellness markets; and wet-laid nonwoven media, specialty and engineered papers, and cellulose acetate fibers for transportation, industrial, agriculture and mining, and aerospace markets. Eastman Chemical Company was founded in 1920 and is headquartered in Kingsport, Tennessee.","employees":13000,"website":"https://www.eastman.com","country":"United States","city":"Kingsport","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Mark J. Costa","title":"Chairman & CEO"},{"name":"Mr. William Thomas McLain Jr.","title":"CFO & Executive VP"},{"name":"Mr. Brad A. Lich","title":"Executive VP & Chief Commercial Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":11.94,"tpe":19.13,"ps":2.295,"pfcf":24.77,"peg":1.72,"pb":2.453,"ev_ebitda":9.424,"rev_growth":0.1625,"eps_growth":0.396,"eps_growth_fwd":0.318,"eps_growth_next":0.1474,"div_yield":0.0086,"roe":0.1295,"roa":0.06934,"de":45.45,"gross_margin":0.3315,"op_margin":0.162,"profit_margin":0.08041,"current_ratio":2.244},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":10.03,"sector":11.94,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":11.64,"sector":19.13,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k"